<http://example.org/kg/lopezmeza_2016/law/lopezmeza_2016_eq5_meta> a mkg:Metadata ;
    mkg:basis "stated" ;
    mkg:description "Antibody accumulation is modeled as the sum of a term proportional to cell growth and a term proportional to viable cell concentration." ;
    mkg:doi "10.1007/s10616-015-9889-2" ;
    mkg:form "ODE" ;
    mkg:hasAssumption [ mkg:quote "We also assumed that a Luedeking–Piret model could describe the kinetics of mAb throughout the entire duration of the cell culture." ;
            mkg:reasoned false ;
            mkg:severity "warning" ;
            mkg:text "The Luedeking–Piret law is assumed to describe antibody kinetics throughout the entire cell-culture duration." ] ;
    mkg:page "4" ;
    mkg:quote "\\mathbf{d}[\\boldsymbol{P}]/\\mathbf{d}\\mathbf{t}=\\mathbf{r}_{\\mathbf{p}}=\\alpha\\mathbf{r}_{\\mathbf{x}}+\\boldsymbol{\\beta}[\\boldsymbol{X}];\\quad\\mathbf{r}_{\\mathbf{x}}=\\mathbf{d}[\\boldsymbol{X}]/\\mathbf{d}\\mathbf{t}" ;
    mkg:status "pending" .

<http://example.org/kg/lopezmeza_2016/lopezmeza_2016_meta> a mkg:Metadata ;
    mkg:completeModel true ;
    mkg:description "The model describes growth, glucose use, and infliximab-biosimilar production by native and recombinant CHO-S cells. It combines first-order growth during the exponential phase with a threshold-modified Monod growth relationship, a cell-yield description of glucose consumption, and a Luedeking–Piret description of antibody formation. The authors developed it using batch cultures in shake flasks at different initial glucose concentrations and temperatures, then evaluated its product-formation description in instrumented batch and fed-batch bioreactors. Cell, glucose, lactate, and active antibody concentrations were measured daily. The authors present the simple kinetic models as tools for understanding and characterizing cell-culture processes, and for applications such as monitoring, control, and optimization." ;
    mkg:doi "10.1007/s10616-015-9889-2" ;
    mkg:form "DAE" ;
    mkg:hasFact [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The viable cell [X] and glucose concentration [S] profiles observed in the exponential phase of batch experiments were fitted to second-order polynomial equations using Excel Software" ;
            mkg:text "Cell and glucose profiles during exponential growth were fitted with second-order polynomials and differentiated to estimate growth and glucose-consumption rates." ;
            mkg:topic "data processing" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Batch cultures were performed using naive (n-CHO) or recombinant cells (r-CHO) in 125-mL shake flasks with 30-mL working volume." ;
            mkg:text "Shake-flask batch cultures used 125-mL flasks with a 30-mL working volume." ;
            mkg:topic "equipment" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The fed-batch protocol consisted of a temperature reduction (31 °C) on the seventh day and five intermittent feed additions (CD EfficientFeed™ B, Invitrogen, Carlsbad, CA, USA) of 10 % the initial volume starting on day 1." ;
            mkg:text "The methods describe fed-batch operation with five intermittent additions of feed, each 10% of the initial culture volume, starting on day 1, and a temperature reduction on day 7." ;
            mkg:topic "feeding" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The values of α and β were chosen to fit several experimental data sets of cell concentration and mAb production profiles." ;
            mkg:text "The authors selected the product-formation coefficients by fitting multiple cell-density and antibody-production data sets and numerically integrating the model." ;
            mkg:topic "estimation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "the rate of product synthesis can be a function of both cellular density ([X]) and the rate of cell growth" ;
            mkg:text "Antibody formation is represented with a Luedeking–Piret model, combining growth-associated and viable-cell-associated production." ;
            mkg:topic "product" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Cultures were seeded at a viable cell density of ~2 × 10⁵ cells/mL and maintained at 33 °C with an 80-rpm rate of agitation. Cultures were supplied with a gas mixture (2 sL/h) consisting of air, oxygen, nitrogen, and carbon dioxide to maintain a dissolved oxygen saturation of 40 %." ;
            mkg:text "Bioreactor cultures were agitated at 80 rpm and supplied with 2 standard L/h of gas to maintain dissolved oxygen at 40% saturation." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The material balance for substrate consumption was assumed to be represented by Eq. 4." ;
            mkg:text "The model relates glucose consumption to cell growth through a cell/substrate yield coefficient." ;
            mkg:topic "substrate use" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "it followed mixed-mode production kinetics, where at any given time the rate of product formation depends on the rate of cell growth and the current viable cell concentration." ;
            mkg:text "The authors describe production by this recombinant line as mixed-mode, with formation related to both growth rate and viable-cell concentration." ;
            mkg:topic "product" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "Glucose and lactate were measured by HPLC with refractive-index detection using an Aminex HPX 87H column and 5 mM sulfuric acid mobile phase." ;
            mkg:topic "measurement" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "The paper places its growth model alongside Monod-like and logistic hybridoma models, Monod and metabolic-flux models, and dynamic metabolic models for nonproducing CHO cells." ;
            mkg:topic "prior models" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "The paper does not report a code or data repository." ;
            mkg:topic "availability" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "Cell density and viability were measured by trypan-blue exclusion using a Guava easyCyte flow cytometer." ;
            mkg:topic "measurement" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The majority of the kinetic models in the literature are categorized as unstructured" ;
            mkg:text "The authors characterize their approach as simple, unstructured kinetic modeling." ;
            mkg:topic "model type" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The proposed parameter values for the Luedeking–Piret model fit reasonably well with several independent experimental data sets in the range of 31–33 °C." ;
            mkg:text "The authors state that the proposed product-formation parameters fit experimental data sets in the range of 31–33 °C." ;
            mkg:topic "scope" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "A Luedeking–Piret-type model (Luedeking and Piret 1959) was proposed for the modeling of antibody production" ;
            mkg:text "The product-formation model is identified as a Luedeking–Piret model, citing Luedeking and Piret 1959." ;
            mkg:topic "prior models" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "The product-formation description was tested on recombinant-cell batch cultures in instrumented bioreactors, and the authors report a good fit using the shake-flask parameter set." ;
            mkg:topic "validation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "A Lineweaver–Burk linearization was used to obtain values for the kinetic parameters" ;
            mkg:text "The growth-kinetic parameters were obtained using Lineweaver–Burk linearization, and a linear regression was accepted only when its r² exceeded 0.97." ;
            mkg:topic "estimation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Interestingly, the Monod-type kinetic values for recombinant cells do not change significantly as a function of temperature" ;
            mkg:text "The fitted Monod parameters for recombinant cells were reported to change little with temperature, whereas those for naive cells changed with temperature." ;
            mkg:topic "growth" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "structured kinetic (Sandadi et al. 2011) and logistic models for r-CHO producing IgG (Goudar et al. 2009); Monte Carlo methodology model for CHO cells producing B1 fusion proteins (Xing et al. 2010); and logistic and regression models for a CHO cell line producing IFN-γ (Farges et al. 2008)." ;
            mkg:text "The authors contrast their approach with earlier recombinant-cell studies using structured kinetic, logistic, Monte Carlo, and regression models, including Sandadi et al. 2011, Goudar et al. 2009, Xing et al. 2010, and Farges et al. 2008." ;
            mkg:topic "prior models" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Experiments were run at different initial substrate concentrations, ranging from 1.2 to 4.8 g/L of glucose (1.2, 2.4, 3.6, and 4.8 g/L)." ;
            mkg:text "Shake-flask batch experiments tested initial glucose concentrations of 1.2, 2.4, 3.6, and 4.8 g/L." ;
            mkg:topic "feeding" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "we used a CHO-S clone engineered in-house (Carrillo-Cocom et al. 2014; González-Leal et al. 2011) to produce a biosimilar of the monoclonal antibody infliximab and its native counterpart" ;
            mkg:text "The model concerns native CHO-S cells and an in-house engineered recombinant CHO-S clone producing an infliximab biosimilar." ;
            mkg:topic "cell lines" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "A single pair of product-formation coefficients did not describe all the 37 °C batch data sets, and the authors suggest lactate inhibition as a possible model improvement." ;
            mkg:topic "limitations" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "All cultures were performed by duplicate with daily sampling. Batch cultures were terminated after 10 days and fed-batch cultures after 20 days." ;
            mkg:text "Bioreactor batch runs lasted 10 days and fed-batch runs lasted 20 days, with duplicate cultures and daily sampling." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "a useful growth model requires the inclusion of a threshold substrate parameter" ;
            mkg:text "The growth relationship is Monod-type but includes a nonzero glucose threshold below which growth is not observed." ;
            mkg:topic "growth" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "All batch cultures were performed in triplicate with daily sampling. Cultures were terminated at day 7 for the r-CHO cell line and at day 10 for the n-CHO line" ;
            mkg:text "Shake-flask cultures were run in triplicate with daily sampling and were stopped after 7 days for recombinant cells or 10 days for naive cells." ;
            mkg:topic "sampling" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Our results suggested that the cell/substrate yield coefficient was not constant, but was a function of the substrate concentration" ;
            mkg:text "The authors found that the cell/substrate yield coefficient varied with glucose concentration rather than remaining constant." ;
            mkg:topic "substrate use" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The time evolution of cell, glucose, lactic acid concentration and monoclonal antibody concentrations was monitored on a daily basis" ;
            mkg:text "The measured time series included viable cell density, glucose, lactic acid, and monoclonal antibody concentrations." ;
            mkg:topic "measurement" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The parameters [S]t and α were kept constant, while μmax, Yx/s, and β were varied iteratively until a good agreement between the [X], [S], and [P] experimental time series and the simulation values was achieved." ;
            mkg:text "For 37 °C recombinant batch data, the authors iteratively adjusted selected growth, yield, and production parameters while holding the threshold and one production coefficient fixed." ;
            mkg:topic "estimation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "These α and β values can be used to accurately reproduce data obtained in experiments where the initial substrate concentration ranges from 2.4 to 4.5 g/L" ;
            mkg:text "The authors report that the product-formation parameters fitted shake-flask data over initial substrate concentrations from 2.4 to 4.5 g/L." ;
            mkg:topic "fit" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Bioreactor-batch and fed-batch cultures were performed only with the recombinant cell line at basal medium concentration. Experiments were performed in 1.6-L bioreactors (DASGIP, Julich, Germany) with 1.0-L working volume." ;
            mkg:text "Instrumented bioreactor experiments used 1.6-L vessels with a 1.0-L working volume and were conducted only with recombinant cells." ;
            mkg:topic "equipment" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "Cultures were seeded at a viable cell density of ~2 × 10⁵ cells/mL and maintained at 33 or 37 °C in an 8 % CO₂ humidified orbital shaking incubator at 125 rpm" ;
            mkg:text "Shake-flask cultures were inoculated at about 2 × 10⁵ viable cells/mL and incubated at 33 or 37 °C, 125 rpm, and 8% CO₂." ;
            mkg:topic "operation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The culture was set to 37 °C for the first 7 days of culture. At day 7, the temperature set point was decreased to 33 °C." ;
            mkg:text "For fed-batch validation, the paper describes a representative instrumented run with a temperature shift from 37 to 33 °C on day 7." ;
            mkg:topic "validation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The cell culture medium consisted of CD Opti CHO (Invitrogen, Carlsbad, CA, USA) supplemented with 8-mM glutamine (Invitrogen, Carlsbad, CA, USA)." ;
            mkg:text "Cultures used CD Opti CHO medium supplemented with 8 mM glutamine." ;
            mkg:topic "medium" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "An enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) was used to quantify the active monoclonal antibody in the collected samples" ;
            mkg:text "The antibody assay quantified active monoclonal antibody in culture samples by ELISA." ;
            mkg:topic "measurement" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "We observed that cell growth was a first-order process (Eq. 1) with respect to cell concentration, at least at the beginning of the exponential growth phase" ;
            mkg:text "The authors treat cell growth as first-order in cell concentration during at least the initial portion of exponential growth." ;
            mkg:topic "growth" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "the viable cell concentration profile [X] was fit to a sixth-order polynomial. The polynomial equation was derived to obtain the experimental cell production rate" ;
            mkg:text "For antibody-production analysis, viable-cell profiles were fitted with a sixth-order polynomial and differentiated to estimate cell-growth rates." ;
            mkg:topic "data processing" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "simple models are particularly appreciated; they are easy to use in real process characterization, online monitoring, process control and process optimization scenarios" ;
            mkg:text "The authors propose simple kinetic models as practical tools for process characterization, online monitoring, process control, and optimization." ;
            mkg:topic "use" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "The paper does not give a consolidated count of model states, equations, or estimated parameters." ;
            mkg:topic "model size" ],
        [ mkg:basis "stated" ;
            mkg:quote "The Luedeking–Piret model previously tested for batch processes (in shake flasks and bioreactors) fit the experimental data" ;
            mkg:text "The authors also applied the batch-derived kinetic parameter set to fed-batch cultures, where they report that the model fit the measured data." ;
            mkg:topic "validation" ],
        [ mkg:basis "inferred" ;
            mkg:text "Lactate was measured and discussed, but the model laws described in the paper do not include a lactate balance or lactate effect." ;
            mkg:topic "lactate" ] ;
    mkg:status "pending" ;
