<http://example.org/kg/link/birol_2002__xing_2010> rdfs:label "Birol 2002 ~ Xing 2010" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Birol 2002 and Xing 2010 are unstructured kinetic models of fed-batch bioreactor cultures, predicting cell growth, substrate use, and product formation. Birol 2002 describes a glucose-fed penicillin fermentation that switches from batch to fed-batch and also models oxygen transfer, pH and temperature control, heat, and culture volume. Xing 2010 describes CHO-cell production of a B1 antibody fusion protein, tracking glucose, glutamine, ammonia, lactate, and viable cell density alongside product; it represents daily feeds and was calibrated by MCMC using large-scale culture runs. Thus they share a culture-kinetics purpose but differ in organism, product, modeled balances, feeding representation, and calibration and validation data." ;
