<http://example.org/kg/link/birol_2002__zentou_2019_andrews> rdfs:label "Birol 2002 ~ Zentou 2019 (Andrews)" ;
    mkg:linkDescription "Birol 2002 and Zentou 2019 (Andrews) are mechanistic microbial-fermentation models that track biomass, substrate consumption, and product formation, so they can be compared as models of fermentation under different conditions. Both include substrate-inhibition effects, though Birol 2002 applies substrate inhibition to penicillin formation while Zentou 2019 (Andrews) uses it in the yeast growth law. Birol 2002 models glucose-fed penicillin production in a batch-to-fed-batch process, with non-growth-associated product formation and additional oxygen, pH, temperature, and energy dynamics. Zentou 2019 (Andrews) models batch molasses fermentation by Saccharomyces cerevisiae, linking ethanol production to growth through yield coefficients and tracking only biomass, substrate, and ethanol." ;
